# Supply-chain policy

Owner: `<team or handle>`. Last reviewed: `<YYYY-MM-DD>`. Review at least every
`<six>` months and after every supply-chain incident. Replace every
`<placeholder>`; delete rows that do not apply and say why.

## Scope

This policy covers every third-party package, GitHub Action, reusable workflow,
container image, pre-commit hook, build backend and CI tool installer used to
build, test or ship `<project>`.

## Admission

- A new runtime dependency needs a completed adoption review approved by
  `<role>` before the manifest changes.
- Prefer the standard library and existing dependencies.
- Package names are verified against the project's own documentation and the
  intended index; internal names resolve only from `<private index>`.

## Constraints and locks

| Surface | Rule | Enforced by |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Application dependencies | locked with hashes in `<uv.lock>` | `<lock freshness check, uv sync --locked>` |
| Published library metadata | bounded ranges; tested build locked | `<pin checker>` |
| Development and CI tools | exact versions in dependency groups | `<pin checker>` |
| GitHub Actions | full commit SHA with version comment | `<zizmor, governance check>` |
| Container images | digest | `<pin checker>` |
| Hooks | frozen commit SHA | `<pin checker>` |

## Audit

- Changed locks are audited before installation with `<pip-audit, OSV-Scanner,
  bun audit>`; the whole lock is audited on a `<daily>` schedule.
- Choose one primary scanner per risk and target. Reuse secret scanning in CI;
  keep workflow security and built-image vulnerability checks separate. Add an
  overlapping scanner only for a documented coverage difference.
- Pull requests run dependency review that fails on `<low>` severity and on
  licenses outside the allow-list.
- Accepted vulnerabilities need an advisory identifier, reachability notes, an
  owner, a tracked issue and an expiry date. Current exceptions:

| Advisory | Package | Reason | Owner | Expires |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `<ID>` | `<name==version>` | `<not reachable because ...>` | `<handle>` | `<YYYY-MM-DD>` |

## Licenses

- Allowed SPDX identifiers live in `<license allow-list file>`; the same list
  configures dependency review.
- Exceptions match the exact observed metadata, record the reviewed license
  file, and expire.

## Updates

- One update bot (`<Dependabot or Renovate>`) owns each manifest.
- Version updates wait `<14>` days after release; security updates do not wait.
- Major upgrades are reviewed one package at a time.

## Build, release and provenance

- Artifacts are built in CI from the lock, never on a workstation.
- Each published artifact has a build provenance attestation bound to its digest.
- SBOM generation is `<required or deferred>` because `<consumer, compliance,
  release-inventory requirement, or deferral reason>`. When required, generate
  `<CycloneDX or SPDX>` and attest it to the released digest. Record whether it
  describes installed contents or a resolved dependency set; a library lock is
  not evidence of dependencies bundled in its wheel.
- Publishing uses `<trusted publishing / OIDC>`; no long-lived upload tokens.

## Incidents

- Report suspected compromise to `<contact>`.
- Follow the incident procedure: freeze, scope, contain, purge, rotate,
  rebuild, notify, learn.
- Credential rotation and public advisories are performed by `<role>`.

## Removal

- Unused dependencies are detected with `<deptry or equivalent>` on
  `<schedule>` and removed after manual confirmation.
